    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f1543eb_0084ecee",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/config.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-07T11:10:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The C `struct` is `__attribute__(packed)` but I don\u0027t think that the C compiler finds any padding to squash given the alignment and order of the fields. So `repr(C)` would probably result in the same representation as `repr(packed)` but would allow Rust code to get references to the fields (currently not possible).\n\nBut, assuming that I\u0027m wrong and that `repr(C)` adds padding, it will result in misaligned fields so I\u0027m using `repr(packed)` to be on the safe side; WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "414b0280_6d6f5e2f",
      "revId": "6e1447625b8552c172a6edb58a4401140be5447d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
